us_order": true, "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01VEoZogy6xbxHsqmvCWHKMw", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" && git log --oneline | head -3; sed -n 13,14p Outline.md | cut -c1-1800", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git pull -q \"$HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git\" && git log --oneline | head -3; sed -n 13,14p Outline.md | cut -c1-1800"]], "output": "```console\n0113098 Outline rev. 13: §1 sentences 4-5 per review #8; ladder diagnostics and rank sensitivity\nfcd0f14 Outline rev. 12: OLB training-side rule result in C4\nb11eec7 Outline rev. 11: OLB results (C7 branch), C4 conditional, title decision, Table 3 verdict, figures as built\n4. We give a closed-form risk for the factor model (floor + design term + remainder) that attributes the error, and test on synthetic data (known truth) and on two real matrices whether it, and a sufficiency rule k*(ε) read from the training models, carry. The design term and the gain from design are predicted well on both. The floor term, which dominates from k ≈ 8, is about 2.5× the prediction on MTEB and about 1.1× on Open LLM Leaderboard (OLB) held-out families (family-stem groups are a heuristic that leaks across checkpoints, so this is the result most exposed to leakage), and 2.5× for OLB's strongest quarter and 8–10× on MTEB's strength and temporal splits; the cause of the misfit is not identified (the diagnostics co-vary with it but no ladder rung reproduces any matrix). The training-side k* rule matches the empirical k* within one grid step when whole groups are held out (MTEB, OLB) and not under a shift in strength or time. T1 is a decomposition that predicts k* where the floor is not mis-specified, not a rule that gives k from the spectrum.\n5. Main result (numbers from the common-target-set runs, matrix named in each clause): the error-vs-k curve on held-out groups; the k that gets within ε points of the floor, for a range of ε; designed selection matters when k is very small: on MTEB (N = 328) random-k is within the coarse margin from about k = 8, on OLB (N = 39) from k = 5 on held-out families and k = 8 on the strongest quarter; beyond that the error sits in the floor; no inference rule tried beats the factor model by more than δ_floor, so better inference is not shown (Table 3); and no k resolves neighbouring models on MTEB (floor ≈ 5 points; the pre-set margin of about 0.1 point, set by adjacent-model gaps, is not reached at any k). The headline k*(ε) is tied to the floor model's capacity (fixed-rank sensitivity: k* at 0.25 × floor on MTEB is 3 / 8 / 20 at rank 4 / 8 / 12 and 32 with the inner-CV rank), so it is reported as a curve with that sensitivity, not as one number.\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "9cf35ead-6e5d-5775-903b-062e8a46d4e3", "at": 1795738616.3667595, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 68265, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5a502f0ed5ce436cef3c3699c00f8c85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "9bd2269c-1d88-5ddc-9ccf-d34fb60e2351", "at": 1795738616.370318, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 68266, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "5a502f0ed5ce436cef3c3699c00f8c85", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "02a98efa-cf99-578b-b38e-dd8309b5ced1", "at": 1795738616.3727882, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 682